line\\versions\\1c8575caf33ea4360ea875366f5bd3b8533ea8c2\\artifacts\\20261027-145146-2c85b8\\cx1\\trace.zip","diagnosis":{"title":"Switching from Write to Preview and back clears the Release notes draft.","root_cause":"Client-side state loss on tab switch. The Write/Preview toggle conditionally unmounts the 'Release notes' textarea and the draft lives only in that unmounted input's local DOM/state rather than in lifted parent state. Switching to Preview destroys the input, switching back to Write creates a fresh empty textarea. No network requests involved, confirmed by empty request_timeline and deterministic reproduction without perturbation.","user_impact":"Users lose their entire release-notes draft by using the intended Draft -> Preview -> Write workflow. They must retype notes, may accidentally Publish empty notes as shown in the screenshot, and lose trust in the editor.","fix":"Lift the draft text to persistent parent state: make the 'Release notes' textarea a controlled component with value/onChange stored outside the Write/Preview panes, and render Preview from that same state. Do not unmount with a changing key; either keep the textarea mounted and hide it with CSS when in Preview, or at minimum restore value from parent state on tab switch.","code_reference":"","confidence":"medium","source":"meta"},"spec_file":"C:\\Users\\Kevin Moritz\\AppData\\Local\\Faultline\\versions\\1c8575caf33ea4360ea875366f5bd3b8533ea8c2\\artifacts\\20261027-145146-2c85b8\\cx1\\faultline-switching-from-write-to-preview-and-back-clears-th.spec.ts","repro_file":"C:\\Users\\Kevin Moritz\\AppData\\Local\\Faultline\\versions\\1c8575caf33ea4360ea875366f5bd3b8533ea8c2\\artifacts\\20261027-145146-2c85b8\\cx1\\repro.json"},{"id":"cx2","title":"Double-activating Publish sends two publish requests.","claim":"Double-activating Publish sends two publish requests.","fault_class":"double_submit","hypothesis_ids":["h3-publish-double","h6-publish-slow-double"],"signature":"max_requests:POST *","o